<title>ITALY: Europe lags in structural reforms - Italy's Fazio.</title>
<headline>Europe lags in structural reforms - Italy's Fazio.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Italy governor Antonio Fazio said on Monday Europe was lagging behind in structural reforms necessary to compete effectively on global markets.</p>
<p>&quot;Europe, in the past decade, has not made the structural changes necessary to respond positively to the challenge of global competition,&quot; Fazio told a convention in Rome.</p>
<p>He said the areas in which Europe was falling behind included labour market flexibility, stripping out public sector inefficiency and innovation in products and production methods.</p>
<p>&quot;We have to make up for this delay since the door to globalisation is now open. That is the backdrop against which our capacity to boost both jobs and wealth will be measured,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 678 2501</p>
</text>
